    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a challenging slate today, but **Colt Keith** stands out as our clear-cut priority start. With a score of 68.51, **Colt Keith** benefits from a massive +19% bump due to the favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez and further elevates his profile by anchoring the lineup at the #1 spot. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces a difficult task against the elite stuff of Paul Skenes, he remains a strong start (62.47) because his speed profile is indispensable in our 5x5 build; he gains a +14% platoon edge and a projected wind boost that keeps his floor well above the marginal threshold. **Kazuma Okamoto** also clears the 60-point barrier, as his power-leaning profile remains stable even against the veteran Chris Bassitt, provided he secures his assumed #5 slot in the order.\n\nNavigating the bottom of our lineup requires caution, particularly with **Caleb Durbin**. While **Caleb Durbin** is a critical engine for our stolen base targets, his score of 40.67 is buoyed primarily by his base projection, as the matchup against Chris Sale is objectively brutal, further complicated by a 35% rain risk that threatens his daily efficiency. **Dillon Dingler** (53.73) and **Chase Meidroth** (53.47) represent our \"marginal\" tier; both are starts by necessity, but they carry limited upside today against capable arms. Notably, the optimizer had to leave **Yordan Alvarez** (57.01) in a high-leverage UTIL spot; despite his elite .422 xwOBA, his matchup against Nathan Eovaldi effectively nullified any platoon advantage, making him a volatile play compared to his usual high-ceiling output. With stars like **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Junior Caminero** all on scheduled team off-days, our bench is devoid of reinforcements, forcing us to lean heavily on this adjusted core to navigate the remaining active games.",
